{# Telephone with a dialling-code prefix.

   Two controls, one field. The select carries the country code and the input
   carries the national number; form-handler.js joins them into a single E.164
   `phone` value on submit, so the backend never sees the split.

   WHY NOT one free-text box: asking for "mobile number with country code" and
   trusting people to add it produces +254…, 254…, 0254…, 0722… in the same
   column. The prefix is the one part a delegate cannot be expected to know for
   their own country and always gets wrong for someone else's.

   WHY NOT libphonenumber: 145KB of dependency to validate a field the
   Secretariat will read by eye. A pattern that rejects nothing legitimate is
   worth more here than one that is strictly correct and rejects a real number.

   Options read "+254 Kenya", dial code FIRST. A native select shows only the
   selected option's text in the closed state and clips it to the control
   width, so "Kenya (+254)" rendered as "Kenya (+..." and hid the one value
   this control exists to display. Country-name-last also keeps the codes in a
   scannable column when the list is open. Ordering stays alphabetical by
   country, which is how people look.

   No flag emoji: they render inconsistently across platforms and several map
   awkwardly to territories.

   Caller sets: fieldId, fieldRequired. Reads `countries`. #}
<div class="form__row form__row--full">
  <label class="label" for="{{ fieldId }}">Mobile number{% if fieldRequired %} <span class="req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>{% endif %}</label>
  <div class="phone">
    {# aria-label, not a visible label: the pair reads as one field, and a
       second visible label would announce as a separate question. #}
    <select class="input phone__code" id="{{ fieldId }}-code" name="phoneCountry"
            aria-label="Country dialling code" autocomplete="tel-country-code">
      {% for c in countries.list %}
      <option value="+{{ c.dial }}" data-code="{{ c.code }}"{% if c.code == countries.default %} selected{% endif %}>+{{ c.dial }} {{ c.name }}</option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>
    <input class="input phone__number" id="{{ fieldId }}" name="phone" type="tel"
           inputmode="tel" autocomplete="tel-national" enterkeyhint="next"
           maxlength="20" placeholder="712 345 678"
           aria-describedby="{{ fieldId }}-hint"{% if fieldRequired %} required{% endif %}>
  </div>
  <span class="form__hint" id="{{ fieldId }}-hint">Without the leading zero.</span>
</div>
